{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And crushed, and smashed, and torn, and cut.</b> In the testicles or in the gland." "<b>Crushed.</b> His testicles are crushed by hand." "<b>Smashed.</b> Crushed more than מָעוּךְ." "<b>Torn.</b> Torn by hand until the threads by which they are suspended are severed, but they are still inside the sac, and the sac was not torn." "<b>And cut.</b> Cut with an instrument and they are still in the sac (Bekhorot 39)." "<b>מעוך.</b> Its Targum is וְדִי מְרִיס — this is its term in Aramaic, a term of crushing." "<b>וכתות.</b> Its Targum is וְדִי רְסִיס, as in ״הַבַּיִת הַגָּדוֹל רְסִיסִים״ (Amos 6) — thin cracks, and likewise ״קָנֶה הַמְרֻסָּס״ (Shabbat 4)." "<b>And in your land you shall not do.</b> This matter is to castrate any animal or beast, even impure — therefore 'in your land' is stated to include everything that is in your land. For if it were not so, we were commanded regarding castration only in the land — but castration is a bodily obligation, and every bodily obligation applies both in the land and outside the land. Therefore 'in your land' must come to include even impure animals."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:51.596754627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}